>> Now it's my understanding that ISA cards should be entered into the
>> SRM console firmware with the "isacfg" command.  However, when I try to
>> add a new device with isacfg, it says, "ISA table is full".
>
>Is your NVRAM jumpered to be read-only?

Newer consoles have incompatible structures for isacfg.  So if you upgraded
the firmware recently, you need to do an "isacfg -init" and then readd the
device information.
